From f51cb47b133b2291887463b1f74eb7b7298bb1ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Lynn <4128043+jefffm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:18:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] APU: restore the full DAC level when reconnecting DMG output

When all DACs are disabled, the DMG mixer holds its coupling-capacitor
charge. The per-channel DAC fade still reaches zero while disconnected.
Applying the existing attack ramp on reconnect therefore subtracts the
full held charge from a fraction of the unchanged source level, creating
a negative pulse and incorrectly discharging the capacitor.

Restore the newly enabled DAC to full level on the all-disabled to
connected transition. Keep the capacitor charge intact so actual source
changes still produce their reconnect step. Retain the existing fades
when another DAC remains enabled and on non-DMG models. No new persistent
state or per-sample work is required.

The pulse appears at all 31 reconnects in the measured NOIZE JAMS passage;
removing it agrees with the original capture and the independent recorded
all-DAC-off/reconnect cases for all four channels. This addresses that
pulse, not all analog onset differences: broader envelope metrics remain
mixed and the 48 kHz capture does not resolve the physical edge latency.

A register-write/sample-callback regression fails 44 checks before this
change and passes afterward, including changed-volume/routing reconnects.
All 24 CGB and other-enabled-DAC control traces are unchanged. The existing
shutdown and mixer regressions pass. A complete original-suite render
preserves the CPU write trace, markers and final screen, and all 337
acoustic packets decode.
---
 Core/apu.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Core/apu.c b/Core/apu.c
index 2c436abb..9d343f31 100644
--- a/Core/apu.c
+++ b/Core/apu.c
@@ -1779,6 +1779,15 @@ void GB_apu_write(GB_gameboy_t *gb, uint8_t reg, uint8_t value)
         reg = GB_IO_WAV_START + gb->apu.wave_channel.current_sample_index / 2;
     }
 
+    bool reconnect_dac = false;
+    if (gb->model == GB_MODEL_DMG_B &&
+        (reg == GB_IO_NR12 || reg == GB_IO_NR22 || reg == GB_IO_NR30 || reg == GB_IO_NR42)) {
+        reconnect_dac = true;
+        unrolled for (unsigned i = 0; i < GB_N_CHANNELS; i++) {
+            reconnect_dac &= !GB_apu_is_DAC_enabled(gb, i);
+        }
+    }
+
     /* Todo: this can and should be rewritten with a function table. */
     switch (reg) {
         /* Globals */
@@ -2252,6 +2261,15 @@ void GB_apu_write(GB_gameboy_t *gb, uint8_t reg, uint8_t value)
         }
     }
     gb->io_registers[reg] = value;
+    if (reconnect_dac) {
+        /* Reconnect the full DAC level to the held coupling capacitor. Starting
+           an attack ramp against its old charge creates a false negative pulse. */
+        unrolled for (unsigned i = 0; i < GB_N_CHANNELS; i++) {
+            if (GB_apu_is_DAC_enabled(gb, i)) {
+                gb->apu_output.dac_discharge[i] = 1;
+            }
+        }
+    }
 }
 
 void GB_set_sample_rate(GB_gameboy_t *gb, unsigned sample_rate)
